/ActualText (Willy Brandt, former German Chancellor, in 1980s as a visual depiction of North-South divide based on GDP per capita, drew a line running from north Mexico, across northern Africa, Middle East, looping around India, China before dropping down to encompass most of East Asia, avoiding Japan, South Korea, Australia and New Zealand.  )
